WEBVTT

00:10:00.055 --> 00:10:01.329
In a structured interview,

00:10:01.353 --> 00:10:03.043
you identify the skills and values

00:10:03.067 --> 00:10:05.185
that are essential
to the job and the team.

00:10:05.209 --> 00:10:07.376
You build a set of questions around those.

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:09.956
And then you ask the same
questions to every candidate

00:10:09.980 --> 00:10:11.656
and score their responses.

00:10:12.117 --> 00:10:15.676
You might be thinking,
"That sounds so robotic and boring,"

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:16.906
but the evidence suggests

00:10:16.930 --> 00:10:19.971
that your accuracy
will often double, or even triple.

00:10:19.995 --> 00:10:22.927
(Music)

00:10:22.951 --> 00:10:25.948
Structured interviews are based
on two kinds of questions:

00:10:25.972 --> 00:10:27.804
behavioral and situational.

00:10:28.172 --> 00:10:30.033
LR: Behavioral questions are generally,